1.bug_scenario:
In Dart code, placing an empty block comment (/**/) before or after a code fragment breaks the syntax highlighting for the code that follows or precedes it. For example:

    /**/main(){print("Hello, World!");}/**/

Here the leading /**/ causes “main” and its body to remain un-highlighted. The empty block comment is being consumed by the doc-comment rule and never properly closed in the general comment rule, so the parser never re-enters the normal Dart mode to highlight the function.
